  "question": {
    "text": "In Dumas' method for estimation of nitrogen 1 g of an organic compound gave 150 mL of nitrogen collected at 300 K temperature and 900 mm Hg pressure. The percentage composition of nitrogen in the compound is _____ $\\%$ (nearest integer).<br />(Aqueous tension at $300 \\mathrm{~K}=15 \\mathrm{~mm} \\mathrm{Hg}$)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "20",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Partial pressure of $\\mathrm{N}_2=(900-15)=885 \\mathrm{~mm} \\mathrm{Hg}$<br />Mole of $\\mathrm{N}_2=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{885}{760} \\times 0.15\\right)}{(0.0821 \\times 300)}=0.0071$ <br />Moles $\\%$ of nitrogen in organic compound<br />$\\begin{aligned}<br />& =\\frac{(0.0071 \\times 28)}{1} \\times 10 \\\\<br>& =19.85 \\%<br />\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
